A||||3||maryjane||2 computer questions||||1||
Z||000000||maryjane||10-13-2001||12:42 PM||||Well, really 3 questions<BR>1: Everytime I get email, a "earthlink download on demand" box appears, telling me I need to dl pan-european software in order to view my mail properly. I know I can get rid of the box by checking the 'never download these progs" box, but what is that & why would I need it. All my mail is domestic, except that from Canadian members here.<BR>2: I frequently get mail w/.txt attachments that contain the formatting, previous recepients, etc, plus a .jpg file. They always state they are in mime format. Anyway, the .jpeg is never readable- just lines & lines of ascii. If the attachment is strictly a .jpg, it comes up no problem. Someone sent me DEC to use to pull the .jpeg out of the .txt attachment but I haven't a clue how to use it and don't want to run some program every time I get an email with an attachment.<BR>3: When I try to go to chat, I get a 'need a java enabled browser' msg. I have java scripting enabled in options as far as I can tell.<BR>IE-5.0<BR>earthlink internet provider<BR>earthlink provided mail reader.<BR>Thanks in advance||||reg||1
Z||000001||Mach10||10-13-2001||01:16 PM||||1) The download box is trying to download additional fonts. It's not where the email originates, it's what font the person uses, whether they add any accents, and what country they have set in the browser.<P>2) That's earthlink's email client being gay. These "custom" email clients don't understand anything other plain text, while everyone else sends in mime (html) Use outlook express...<P>3) Again, earthlink is being chromasomally challenged. Sounds like they are using an older version of the Java scripting which doesn't recognize new scripts. <P>In summary: Don't ever use bundled "custom" software if you can possibly avoid it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR>"Duct Tape is Good to Mach 3"<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.AnimierteGif.de/Smilies/Smilies_boese/smileystooges.gif">   <IMG SRC="http://www.AnimierteGif.de/Smilies/Smilies_boese/totalsmash.gif">   <IMG SRC="http://www.AnimierteGif.de/Smilies/Smilies_boese/space_cowboy_hat.gif">   <IMG SRC="http://www.AnimierteGif.de/Smilies/Smilies_boese/smashfreakB.gif">   <IMG SRC="http://www.AnimierteGif.de/Smilies/Smilies_boese/smileystooges.gif">   <IMG SRC="http://www.AnimierteGif.de/Smilies/Smilies_boese/sa38.gif"> ||||reg||12
Z||000002||maryjane||10-13-2001||01:38 PM||||Any chance that doing the suggested down load will cure the mime format problem? I've avoided outlook express because I understand many viruses target it. I'm running Norton, but still cautious. I'll have to give it a try tho. You know how it is with old dogs & new tricks. thanks||||reg||1
Z||000003||Mach10||10-13-2001||01:54 PM||||It's fairly easy to bullet-proof OE.<P>Go to tools --&gt; Options --&gt; Read and turn off automatically open messages<BR>Next, OK out of that, and go to View --&gt; Layout, and disable the preview pane. <P>The other thing is to periodically download MS's updates... They close up security holes where they find them...<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"> I misread the Q about java errors.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"> Sounds like a corrupt virtual machine. Reinstall OE.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||10
